    {
      "def": "a long vegetable with dark green skin and light green flesh, that is usually eaten raw 黄瓜",
      "ex": [
        {
          "s": "Things like kale ribs, fish collars, rejected sweet potatoes, and cucumber butts were all re-appropriated and, with the help of a number of good chefs, turned into excellent cuisine.",
          "src": "2025新高考II卷·阅读理解D",
          "cat": "gaokao",
          "year": 2025,
          "t": "像羽衣甘蓝梗、鱼颈肉、被挑拣出的红薯和黄瓜屁股这类东西，都被重新利用，并在几位好厨师的帮助下，变成了极好的菜肴。"
        },
        {
          "s": "For example, He is as cool as a cucumber.",
          "src": "外研社B6 U3",
          "cat": "waiyan",
          "year": "",
          "t": "例如，他冷静得像根黄瓜（比喻镇定自若）。"
        },
        {
          "s": "The most popular cricket snacks are finger foods like biscuits and cucumber sandwiches.",
